ter approval the editor downloads a print-ready\nA4 or A5 PDF. Backend is a Google Apps Script over a Sheet and Drive; the\npage runs in browser-only demo mode until it's connected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019WLNtRWLXS2QmFFoPaeKLP","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedsaheerahmed786-rgb/Sahir/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/syedsaheerahmed786-rgb/Sahir/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1236702,"client_id":"Iv23liqTIFEtdIu6Vn1r","slug":"claude","node_id":"A_kwHOBIuudM4AEt7e","owner":{"login":"anthropics","id":76263028,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjc2MjYzMDI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76263028?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthropics/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Claude","description":"Run Claude Code from your GitHub Pull Requests and Issues to respond to reviewer feedback, fix CI errors, or modify code, turning it into a virtual teammate that works alongside your development pipelines.\r\n\r\nThis is built on the publicly available Claude Code SDK.","external_url":"https://anthropic.com/claude-code","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/claude","created_at":"2025-04-30T17:54:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T19:04:00Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","discussion","discussion_comment","issues","issue_comment","merge_group","merge_queue_entry","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","release","repository_ruleset","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow/issues/216","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow/issues/216/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow/issues/216/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow/issues/216/events","html_url":"https://github.com/emmyfong/snow/pull/216","id":6018098479,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVAcqHs8AAAABKf8kNw","number":216,"title":"feat(convstore): save conversations so a crash never loses them","user":{"login":"emmyfong","id":89320276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MzIwMjc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89320276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong","html_url":"https://github.com/emmyfong","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emmyfong/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-24T22:04:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T22:08:08Z","closed_at":"2026-10-24T22:08:06Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow/pulls/216","html_url":"https://github.com/emmyfong/snow/pull/216","diff_url":"https://github.com/emmyfong/snow/pull/216.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/emmyfong/snow/pull/216.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-24T22:08:06Z"},"body":"<!-- One line for the epic and one for each sub-issue this PR completes. -->\nCloses #186\nCloses #97\nCloses #98\nCloses #99\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add `internal/convstore`: one append-only JSON Lines file per conversation in `~/.snow/conversations`, private to the user.\n- #97 Append.\n  - `Create` makes the file with `O_EXCL` and writes the meta record before it returns. `Writer` resumes an existing file.\n  - Each record is one whole line, flushed with `fsync` before `Append` returns.\n  - Partial text of a streaming reply is written at most once per second, with the latest text.\n  - A record after a torn line starts on a new line. One conversation has one live writer per `Store`.\n  - IDs are the UTC time plus 8 hex characters (`20261023-191500-a1b2c3d4`). `CheckID` refuses anything that is not a safe file name on every OS.\n- #98 Load. Load never writes, renames, or deletes the file.\n  - A torn last line is dropped. A damaged line is marked in place with a `Damaged` record.\n  - Trailing partial text becomes a reply marked \"cut off\".\n  - A tool call with no saved result gets a \"result lost\" stand-in, so the next request to the provider is valid.\n  - `MidTurn` tells the caller to show the turn as interrupted.\n  - Load returns its problems, and the caller logs them.\n- #99 List: per folder and shell profile, newest first, with title, model, last activity, and turn count.\n  - A file that cannot be read is listed with its error and kept.\n  - No index. 1000 files of 100 KB list in 0.11 s on Linux and 0.25 s on Windows (warm cache). The first open of new files on Windows is slower (about 1.5 s for 1000), because of antivirus.\n- Design choices, approved in the plan:\n  - `convstore` has its own record types and never imports `internal/provider` (depguard). The agent loop (#100) converts.\n  - Tool calls are blocks inside the assistant record, in vendor order. They are not a separate record type.\n- Deviation from #98: a last line with no newline that still decodes as whole JSON is kept, not dropped.\n- `internal/private`: `SyncDir` is exported. `privatetest.OwnerOnly` checks a 0600/0700 mode, or a one-entry Windows ACL. The credential test uses it.\n- AGENTS.md lists `convstore`. depguard keeps it out of the client. The issue-handler skill says how to reopen an epic after a partial merge.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- Review wave: 3 reviewers. All 18 findings are fixed in this branch. One out-of-scope note is not fixed: five packages build the `~/.snow` path. A follow-up can share it.\n- `go build ./...`: pass. `CGO_ENABLED=0` builds for Windows and macOS: pass.\n- `golangci-lint run ./...` (v2.15.0), linux, windows, darwin: 0 issues.\n- `go test` and `go test -race` on `internal/convstore`, `internal/private/...`, `internal/credential`: pass.\n- Windows test binaries for the same packages: pass. This includes the kill tests (`TerminateProcess`), the owner-only ACL check, and an unreadable file (held open with no sharing).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests ship with the change (bug fixes start with a failing test).\n- [x] Comments follow AGENTS.md: doc comments on exported names, inline only for the why.\n- [x] The PR title is a Conventional Commit.\n- [x] `.context/CONTEXT.md` is updated.\n\nCo-authored by Claude Code.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow/issues/216/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/emmyfong/snow/issues/216/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/metaodi/halloween-map/issues/3","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/metaodi/halloween-map","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/metaodi/halloween-map/issues/3/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/metaodi/halloween-map/issues/3/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/metaodi/halloween-map/issues/3/events","html_url":"https://github.com/metaodi/halloween-map/pull/3","id":6018097811,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVWKagc8AAAABKf8iIg","number":3,"title":"Karte: Swiss-Style-Tiles (OSM Switzerland) statt Standard-OSM","user":{"login":"metaodi","id":538415,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODQxNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538415?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi","html_url":"https://github.com/metaodi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metaodi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type"